-- REVIEW-ONLY, DBA APPROVAL REQUIRED. NOT applied by tests or application code.
-- PostgreSQL privileges are additive: revoking from a runtime role does not
-- remove privileges inherited from PUBLIC/other roles. On a DEDICATED database,
-- review all legitimate users before applying these database-wide changes.
-- app_database is the psql identifier variable, not a URL/password.
-- Existing workloads relying on TEMP or public CREATE may break; schedule and
-- approve separately. Never apply this blindly to a shared/provider database.
BEGIN;
REVOKE CREATE, TEMPORARY ON DATABASE :"app_database" FROM PUBLIC;
REVOKE CREATE ON SCHEMA public FROM PUBLIC;
COMMIT;
-- Also inspect/revoke unintended direct or inherited grants on runtime LOGIN
-- principals and all other writable schemas. The runtime must not own objects,
-- hold migration/admin membership, or execute unsafe SECURITY DEFINER functions.
-- Without this boundary, app-schema DDL is denied but TEMP table DDL may remain.
